module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.fold_rewrite_regression_visible_only_at_whole_route_identity_diff

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data fold_rewrite_regression_visible_only_at_whole_route_identity_diff: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "fold_rewrite_regression_visible_only_at_whole_route_identity_diff" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a rewrite of a SHARED reader inside a lowering fold changes the answer every OTHER caller of that reader receives, and the rewrite's own controls exercise only the caller the rewrite was about -- so its claims go green, its reviewers approve, and the refusals it introduces elsewhere land on files no claim of the change compiles (DESIGN section 3, a witness discriminates at one interface; the pairing obligation is what this class slips past)",
    "SPECIMEN, 2026-09-23. gunbc#12145 closed the sequence arm of `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_operand_ref_optional` (a sequence operand is never narrowed) and proved it with `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.sequence_operand_resolve_refusal`, green. The same reader was the value reader of two other callers: the match scrutinee and the call argument. For a call scrutinee or a lambda argument those callers had been receiving the callee or the parameter atom, a silent truncation. From #12145 on they got Absent, and each refused its whole file: `body_lowering_reason_match_arm_navigation_refused` and `body_lowering_reason_call_argument_unread`. The operator bisect over the native lane (`gunbc test //v2/test/parse/expression_bodied_fn_decl_parse:all`, parent 2de78893dfe against ada85b9452b) counted 81 new file refusals, none removed, including gen-one's first fatal emitting `v2.compiler.compile`",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: every control of the change is green; the regression surfaces only as file refusals on the native lane's ingest population, and it is visible only as an identity-grain diff of that population's refusals between parent and child, never as a count on the child alone; the new refusal cause names a caller the diff did not mention",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The refusals were loud and typed, so nothing was silently wrong, but they reached main because no gate compares the lane's refusal identities across a change. CEILING: mechanically preventable. A required step that diffs the native lane's file-refusal identities between the merge base and the candidate, and fails on any added identity, is decidable over a closed, discovered population. NEXT TRIGGER: that identity diff enrolled on the required path. The repair of this specimen reads every value-position caller through `body_lower_value_lowered`: call arguments and match scrutinees in gunbc#12173 (claim `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal`), the operator-operand fallback and function-value arguments in its follow-up (claim `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.value_position_whole_read`, which asserts the lowered call's shape on the production route). The follow-up also found a THIRD caller of the same reader (`body_lower_operator_operand`, 6 files), which the parent-vs-child identity diff surfaced and the first hotfix's own claims did not. That repair closes this instance, not the class"
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
